\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus, Thy far-extended fame
\par My dropping soul exults to hear;
\par Thy name, Thy all-restoring name,
\par Is music in a sinner's ear.
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par \'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Sinners of old Thou didst receive
\par With comfortable words and kind,
\par Their sorrows cheer, their wants relieve,
\par Heal the diseased, and cure the blind.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And art Thou not the Saviour still,
\par In every place and age the same?
\par Hast Thou forgot Thy gracious skill,
\par Or lost the virtue of Thy name!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Faith in Thy changeless name I have;
\par The good, the kind physician, Thou
\par Art able now our souls to save,
\par Art willing to restore them now.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Wouldst Thou the body's health restore,
\par And not regard the sin-sick soul?
\par The sin-sick soul Thou lov'st much more,
\par And surely Thou shalt make it whole.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. All my disease, my every sin,
\par To Thee, O Jesus, I confess;
\par In pardon, Lord, my cure begin,
\par And perfect it in holiness.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

